Residual of "phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Move pipe_clk on/off to common" for 7.2.

Linux 7.2 already carries Val Packett's mainline change (lkml.org/lkml/2026/2/28/1653):
pipe_clk prepare/enable moved into qmp_combo_com_init(), disable/unprepare into
qmp_combo_com_exit(). The only piece still missing is the USB power-on timeout
path, which keeps a `goto err_disable_pipe_clk` that disables a clock this
function no longer enables -> the gcc_usb3_prim_phy_pipe_clk double-unprepare
seen on DP hotplug / mode transitions. Drop that error path; com_exit() owns the
clock now.

--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -3910,15 +3910,10 @@
 			PHY_INIT_COMPLETE_TIMEOUT);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(qmp->dev, "phy initialization timed-out\n");
-		goto err_disable_pipe_clk;
+		return ret;
 	}

 	return 0;
-
-err_disable_pipe_clk:
-	clk_disable_unprepare(qmp->pipe_clk);
-
-	return ret;
 }

 static int qmp_combo_usb_power_off(struct phy *phy)
